## Red-checks (reverted, observed, restored)
1. AC-2 error/done store removed → both AC-2 tests fail (`409 busy` on the next POST).
2. AC-3 semaphore removed → `test_the_handler_thread_cap_closes_the_extra_connection_and_releases_at_timeout` fails ("did not take one slot per held connection").
3. AC-3 stream cap removed → `test_a_fifth_stream_on_one_job_is_429_and_a_freed_slot_admits_another` fails (`streams == 0`).
4. AC-4 filter replaced with identity → `test_a_refused_unknown_path_is_logged_as_unknown_not_echoed` fails (token on stderr).
5. AC-5 `PS = "ps"` → `test_resident_osaurus_pids_never_runs_a_ps_found_on_path` fails (fake executed).
6. AC-1 mode/chmod removed → both `test_ensure_app_support_*` tests fail (0755 instead of 0700).

## Verification
- Baseline: `1164 passed` → final: `1188 passed in 45.34s`.
- No commit made. Only the allowed files changed (`git status` shows the pre-existing `.paul` edits untouched).
- No runtime, model, download, real port, real `~/.osaurus` or real Application Support was touched; app subprocess tests now run with a scratch `HOME`.

## Unsure / judgement calls
- `hardware` imports `SYSCTL` from `sample.py` rather than spelling it again; `sample.py` was out of scope and already owned the constant. If you wanted hardware to own it, sample would need editing.
- The installed-app layout is simulated by pointing `ohyesmlx.__file__` at a read-only tmp package tree, not by a real `pip install`.
- `_served_path` runs only on guard refusals (the only `_log_refusal` caller); an authorised 404 writes no line at all, so there is nothing to filter there.
- The handler-cap test waits on `BoundedSemaphore._value` (CPython private) for determinism.

